    [Doc][KVPP] Refresh supported combinations and execution constraints (#18770)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    Refresh the KVPP user guide and feature compatibility matrix to match
    current support. Only these two Markdown files are changed.
    
    - Correct graph support to PIECEWISE and remove the obsolete eager-only
    requirement.
    - Document all speculative decoding methods with fixed K; dynamic K has
    not been validated. Mark Eagle3 compatible in the feature matrix.
    - Delete the obsolete PCP + P/D + KVPP and PCP + pooling + KVPP
    exception rows; PCP, P/D, and pooling already have their own support
    entries.
    - Keep MultiConnector under KV transfer configuration and remove the
    stale unreleased-connector statement.
    
    - Remove internal broadcast, prefetch, and cache-buffer details so the
    guide focuses on supported scenarios, configuration, and measured
    performance.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    No runtime behavior changes; documentation only.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    - `git diff --check` passed.
    - Verified the final PR diff contains exactly the KVPP user guide and
    feature matrix.
    - Checked removal of the obsolete PCP combination rows and redundant
    eager/graph instructions, verified fixed-K support wording, and parsed
    the JSON configuration example.
    - Reviewed the guide against current KVPP validation and
    connector/cache-placement implementation. No NPU tests or full
    documentation build were run for this Markdown-only update.
    
    
    
    
    
    
    
